### Distributed tracing (unit 5.8)
### Start with request-level logs: docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.labs.yaml up --build -d
### Passwords come from .env.

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Login
# @name userLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo-user",
  "password": "<DEMO_USER_PASSWORD from .env>"
}

@userToken = {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 2. A request that continues a known trace. Then search the gateway and catalog logs for
### 4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736: both show it, with different span ids.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
traceparent: 00-4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01

### 3. Without trace context the gateway starts a new trace. Find its id in the gateway log line
### (the second bracket group after the thread name) and search the catalog log for it.
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
